{"entity":{"id":"hb:odrysian-kingdom@0","name":"Odrysian Kingdom","dataset":"basemaps","kind":"kingdom"},"territories":[{"id":846,"name":"Odrysian Kingdom","set_id":"hb_-1","class":"dependency","valid_from":0,"valid_to":100,"snapshot_held":1,"area_km2":67519.16731460179,"border_precision":1,"capital_name":null,"sovereign":"Roman Empire","sovereign_note":"As mapped by Historical Basemaps (world_bc1.geojson)","modern_name":"Turkey (Ottoman Empire)","min_lon":24.0809616391434,"min_lat":40.044654451326174,"max_lon":29.081099543181605,"max_lat":43.16314989680194,"source_file":"world_bc1.geojson","source_row":null}],"identities":[{"qid":"Q870517","from_t":0,"to_t":46,"method":"name-label+date","confidence":0.95,"label":"Odrysian kingdom","description":"union of Thracian tribes and kingdoms (5th century BC to 1st century AD)","inception":-459,"dissolved":46,"enwiki":"Odrysian kingdom","summary":"The Odrysian kingdom (; Ancient Greek: Βασίλειον Ὀδρυσῶν) was an ancient Thracian state that thrived between the early 5th century BC and the early 3rd / late 1st century BC. Located in present-day Bulgaria, southeastern Romania (Northern Dobruja), northern Greece and European Turkey, it was a tribal amalgam dominated by the Odrysians that was the first large political entity to develop in the eastern Balkans. Before the foundation of Seuthopolis in the late 4th century it had no fixed capital.\nThe Odrysian kingdom was founded by king Teres I, exploiting the collapse of the Persian presence in Europe due to failed invasion of Greece in 480–79. Teres and his son Sitalces pursued a policy of expansion, making the kingdom one of the most powerful of its time."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q870517","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q1291235","value_label":"Seuthopolis","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Seuthopolis"},{"qid":"Q870517","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q36793","value_label":"Thracian","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"pr